=== TITLE: 2D Echocardiography & Color Doppler (Normal) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL 2D ECHOCARDIOGRAPHY AND COLOR DOPPLER STUDY.
- Normal LV systolic function (LVEF: 60 - 65%).
- Normal chamber dimensions and valvular morphology.
- No regional wall motion abnormality (RWMA) at rest.
- No pericardial effusion or intracardiac clot / vegetations.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: 2D ECHOCARDIOGRAPHY WITH COLOR DOPPLER

MEASUREMENTS:
- Left Ventricle (LVIDd): 4.4 cm (Normal: 3.5 - 5.5 cm)
- Left Ventricle (LVIDs): 2.8 cm (Normal: 2.5 - 4.0 cm)
- Interventricular Septum (IVSd): 0.9 cm (Normal: 0.6 - 1.1 cm)
- LV Posterior Wall (LVPWd): 0.9 cm (Normal: 0.6 - 1.1 cm)
- Ejection Fraction (EF): 62 %
- Left Atrium (LA Dimension): 3.2 cm (Normal: 2.0 - 4.0 cm)
- Aortic Root (Ao Dimension): 2.9 cm (Normal: 2.0 - 3.7 cm)

OBSERVATIONS:
- LEFT VENTRICLE: Normal in size. Good global LV systolic function. No regional wall motion abnormality (RWMA) detected at rest. Normal myocardial thickness.
- LEFT ATRIUM: Normal in size and morphology.
- RIGHT ATRIUM & RIGHT VENTRICLE: Normal chamber dimensions. RV systolic function is normal (TAPSE: 22 mm).
- MITRAL VALVE: Normal leaflet mobility and thickness. No MR / MS. Normal E/A ratio.
- AORTIC VALVE: Trileaflet, opens well during systole. No AR / AS.
- TRICUSPID VALVE: Structurally normal. Trivial TR noted. Estimated PASP is normal (< 25 mmHg).
- PULMONARY VALVE: Normal morphology. No pulmonary arterial hypertension (PAH).
- INTERATRIAL & INTERVENTRICULAR SEPTUM: Intact on color Doppler.
- PERICARDIUM: Normal thickness. No pericardial effusion.